ns.WhatsNew = {
    { version = "2.4.5", text = "Launch-day fixes: whisper tabs, Target of Target, and nothing reloads your UI in a fight.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Chat: a new whisper tab no longer opens with an empty window, and whisper tabs now fade in and out like your other chat windows.\n• Target of Target and Target of Focus: health and power now update during the fight, not only when the target changes.\n• Reload questions: if one was closed during combat, pressing Enter could still reload the UI. Enter now opens the chat as usual, and a dialog shown in combat no longer blocks your movement keys.\n• Settings: closing the window in combat no longer leaves a clickable |cffffffffReload now|r button on screen.\n• Quest Tracker: |cffffffffMinimize in combat|r now works.\n• Raid frames: Missing Buffs no longer throws errors when you die during a boss fight, and no longer marks members who are too far away to check.\n• Raid frames: your own frame no longer flickers faded, and members whose range can't be checked are no longer faded.\n• Quality of Life: turning the module off now puts back the game settings it changed (enemy nameplates, camera zoom, tutorials). Sync Blizz UI no longer copies \"enemy nameplates off\" from Combat Plates to your other characters.\n• Radial Menu: |cffffffffCreate macro|r now allows up to 30 character macros, and a Toggle keybind with no radial left no longer errors.\n• Fake Cooldown Manager: bars no longer stay clickable after dropping a spell during combat.\n• Target frame: the Elite & Rare icon follows changes, and an old ready check mark no longer shows on a new target.\n• XP bar: hides more reliably when you reach max level." },
    { version = "2.4.4", text = "Share your FlareUI profile as a text string.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• Profiles: |cffffffffExport|r and |cffffffffImport|r buttons under the profile options. Export shows the profile in use as a string to copy; Import takes a pasted string and adds it as a new profile (your current one is never overwritten). Radial menus and Blizzard's Edit Mode layouts aren't included.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Profiles: the profile options sit in a |cffffffffProfile|r section.\n• About: the note on copying links now ends the thanks line.\n• Radial Menu: |cffffffffGame Menu|r is gone from the Panels library (it couldn't open the game menu from a radial)." },
    { version = "2.4.3", text = "Party frames in a row again, a modern combo bar for FlareUI Style, and Only My Buffs on the player frame.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• Party frames: |cffffffffOrientation|r is back (Vertical or Horizontal), between Style and Growth. In a row, Growth reads Right or Left. Each frame leaves room for its side auras, a pet or target on its right, and the ring in FlareUI and Forever Style.\n• Target frame, FlareUI Style: |cffffffffModern Combo Points|r at the bottom of Look (off by default). The combo points show as Addon Style's bar along the top of the health bar instead of gems round the portrait.\n• Player frame: |cffffffffOnly My Buffs|r right below Aura Size (off by default): only the buffs you cast on yourself." },
    { version = "2.4.2", text = "A bigger minimap without a bulkier frame, and a cast bar switch on the target and focus frames.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• Minimap: |cffffffffMap Size|r in Edit Mode, in a panel under the minimap's dialog. It grows or shrinks the map itself; the border, header and buttons keep their size. Blizzard's Size slider is now called |cffffffffScale|r and still scales the whole minimap.\n• Target and focus frames: a |cffffffffCast Bar|r switch at the top of the Cast Bar section (on by default), like the one on party and boss frames.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Target and focus frames: Cast Bar Texture now sits right below Cast Bar Position.\n• Party and boss frames: Cast Bar Texture now sits above Cast Bar Height." },
    { version = "2.4.1", text = "Aura ordering on every aura frame, and the swipe choice back on Buffs & Debuffs.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• |cffffffffAura Ordering|r, a new section right below Auras in Edit Mode on every unit frame with auras: player, target, focus, pet and their targets, party, raid, main tanks and boss frames.\n• Aura Ordering: |cffffffffSort By|r (Default, Order Applied, Time Left or Name), |cffffffffReverse Order|r, and |cffffffffYour Auras First|r (with Time Left or Name). Default keeps Blizzard's order; nothing changes until you pick one. On party, raid and boss frames the buff and debuff rows are sorted; Bigger Boss Debuffs, dispel icons and the big defensive keep their order.\n• Buffs & Debuffs: the same Aura Ordering options in a new section of their settings page (Order Applied by default, as before). The icon shape and timer options now sit under |cffffffffGeneral|r.\n• Buffs & Debuffs: |cffffffffSwipe|r is back in General: Over the icon, Around the border, Both or None.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• The aura swipe now runs over the icon and its border together (|cffffffffBoth|r): the default on Buffs & Debuffs, and on every unit frame aura (player, target, focus, pet, party, raid, main tanks and boss).\n• Buffs & Debuffs, Around the border: a slightly thicker ring and richer border colours." },
